  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,000eb (Very Expensive)</p>\n<p><em>Not the most powerful cyberdeck kit on the market, but capable of performing multiple tasks – even if it does require a little patience.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Neuroport Cyberdeck Port Operating System.</strong> The Neuroport Cyberdeck Port can now only accept a Militech Paraline Cyberdeck, one of which is provided with purchase of this Operating System.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Militech Paraline</strong> is a Cyberdeck with 14 slots that can install Programs or Hardware. While using this Cyberdeck, the user has one less NET Action every Turn (Minimum 1).</p>\n<p><strong>Enhances:</strong> Neuroport Cyberdeck Port<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> 0 (Cyberware Enhancement)</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Corgo's required content includes the Edgerunners Mission Kit and Interface RED, and this parent piece comes from there rather than from Cyberpunk RED - Core, which ships no item for it. Make the parent yourself before installing this into it.</li>\n<li>Every Operating System is incompatible with every other Operating System and with the base cyberware it is for: none of them can be installed while another OS, or that OS's own base cyberware, is anywhere in the user's body or in a worn apparatus they're connected to. The sheet doesn't enforce that.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Operating Systems &gt; Cyberdeck Port Operating Systems).</em></p>"
  },
